Third-party software in the published images
--------------------------------------------
Every image is assembled from Wolfi packages (https://packages.wolfi.dev) and official Python sources
(https://www.python.org), each under its upstream license; the Wolfi build recipes are Apache License 2.0
(https://github.com/wolfi-dev/os). The SPDX SBOM attached to every image and every GitHub release lists
the license of each package. Among them:

- Python: Python Software Foundation License Version 2 (PSF-2.0).
- pip, setuptools: MIT License / Apache License 2.0.
- glibc: LGPL-2.1-or-later. OpenSSL: Apache License 2.0.
- In both runtime and development images: busybox (GPL-2.0-only), bash (GPL-3.0-or-later).
- In the development images also: GCC (GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception),
  make (GPL-3.0-or-later), git (GPL-2.0-only).

Source code for the GPL and LGPL packages is available from their upstream projects and from the
Wolfi build recipes, which name the exact upstream source and version of every package. On request,
we provide the corresponding source of any package in an image we published, for three years after
that image's release.

